# Security Rules - Greek ERP/CRM System

## Core Security Framework

- **Authentication**: JWT with refresh tokens, 2FA for admin accounts
- **Authorization**: RBAC with fine-grained permissions and company isolation
- **Encryption**: AES-256 for data at rest, TLS 1.3 for data in transit
- **Password Policy**: NIST 800-63B compliant with Greek character support
- **Session Management**: Secure session handling with timeout policies
- **GDPR Compliance**: Full compliance for Greek personal data protection
- **Audit Logging**: Comprehensive audit trail for all business operations

## Authentication Standards

- **JWT Tokens**: 15-minute access tokens, 7-day refresh tokens
- **Multi-Factor**: 2FA required for admin and financial roles
- **Password Security**: Bcrypt hashing, never plain text storage
- **Token Management**: Secure token storage and refresh mechanisms
- **Company Context**: MANDATORY company_id in all tokens

## Authorization & Access Control

- **RBAC Model**: Role-based permissions (business_entities:create, invoices:edit)
- **Company Isolation**: MANDATORY on ALL endpoints and data access
- **Permission Granularity**: Fine-grained business operation permissions
- **Admin Separation**: Super admin vs company admin role separation
- **Greek Financial**: Special permissions for AFM/VAT/AADE operations

## Data Protection & Encryption

- **Sensitive Data**: Encrypt AFM, personal info, bank details at rest
- **Key Management**: Environment-based encryption keys, never hardcoded
- **Database Security**: Row-level security for company isolation
- **Transport Security**: TLS 1.3 for all client-server communication
- **Field-Level**: Encrypt specific columns containing Greek business data

## GDPR & Privacy Compliance

- **Consent Management**: Record and track data processing consent
- **Data Portability**: Export capabilities for business entity data
- **Right to Erasure**: Anonymization workflows for data deletion
- **Audit Trail**: Complete logging of data access and modifications
- **Greek Context**: Special handling for Greek personal data laws

## Input Validation & Sanitization

- **Greek Characters**: Proper validation and sanitization for Greek text
- **AFM Validation**: Checksum validation for Greek tax numbers
- **DOY Validation**: Valid Greek tax office code verification
- **SQL Injection**: Parameterized queries, never string concatenation
- **XSS Prevention**: Output encoding and CSP headers

## Security Monitoring & Auditing

- **Audit Logging**: Log ALL business operations with user attribution
- **Suspicious Activity**: Monitor brute force, unusual access patterns
- **Greek Data Access**: Special monitoring for AFM/VAT data exports
- **Failed Attempts**: Rate limiting and lockout mechanisms
- **Security Alerts**: Automated alerts for security incidents

## API Security Standards

- **Rate Limiting**: Protect endpoints from abuse and DDoS
- **CORS Configuration**: Proper origin restrictions
- **Input Validation**: Validate all inputs, especially Greek business data
- **Error Handling**: Never expose internal details in error responses
- **API Keys**: Secure management of external service credentials

## Session & State Management

- **Redis Sessions**: Secure session storage with expiration
- **CSRF Protection**: Token-based CSRF prevention
- **Session Timeout**: Automatic logout for inactive sessions
- **Concurrent Sessions**: Limit simultaneous sessions per user
- **Company Context**: Maintain company isolation in session state

## Greek Compliance Security

- **AFM Protection**: Encrypted storage and secure transmission
- **AADE Integration**: Secure API communication with Greek tax authority
- **VAT Data**: Protect tax calculation and rate information
- **Business Secrets**: Secure storage of Greek business credentials
- **Compliance Audit**: Greek tax authority audit requirements

## Infrastructure Security

- **Environment Separation**: Clear boundaries between dev/staging/production
- **Secrets Management**: Secure storage of API keys and credentials
- **Database Security**: Connection encryption and access controls
- **Backup Security**: Encrypted backups with access controls
- **Network Security**: VPC, firewalls, and intrusion detection

## What NOT to Do

- ❌ Never store passwords in plain text or with weak hashing
- ❌ Don't skip company isolation in any endpoint
- ❌ Never hardcode encryption keys or secrets in code
- ❌ Don't allow SQL injection through unvalidated inputs
- ❌ Never expose sensitive Greek business data in logs
- ❌ Don't skip input validation for Greek characters
- ❌ Never disable HTTPS in production environments
- ❌ Don't ignore GDPR consent requirements
- ❌ Never skip audit logging for financial transactions
- ❌ Don't trust client-side validation alone

